 ## Overview
-Mitchell-Netravali cubic interpolation is a family of C0 and C1 continuous cubic filters defined by parameters B and C, used to reconstruct volume data while preventing high-frequency leakage artifacts [S1]. It distinguishes itself from simpler schemes by offering a tunable trade-off between blurring and ringing, and from fixed B-splines by allowing the generation of Catmull-Rom splines [S1]. It builds on [Fast tri-cubic interpolation](848-fast-tri-cubic-interpolation.md) by providing the specific kernel weights for the convolution sum.
